    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Implement Hybrid Logic\r\n\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Protect the user from errors by trying to fetch live data first, then falling back to your safety net if it fails.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Clean up the code: Delete the line renderBackup(); from the bottom of your code.\r\n\r\n2. Create an async arrow function named `fetchEvents`. Inside, add a `try...catch` block.\r\n\r\n3. Inside the `try` block:\r\n\r\n    * Call `updateStatus()` with the message `\"Online. Showing Live Events.\"`\r\n    * Use `fetch()` to get data from the `apiEndpoint`\r\n    * Loop through the results and call `createLiveCard()` for each event, passing in its title, location_name, and start.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Inside catch:\r\n\r\n    * Call `updateStatus()` with the message `\"Offline Mode. Showing Local Events.\"`\r\n    * Call your `renderBackup()` function.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Add an event listener so that clicking the \"Get Live Events\" button runs your `fetchEvents` function.",
